WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.219 --> 00:00:03.802
(upbeat, industrial music)

00:00:05.219 --> 00:00:07.019
- Working out has been
a huge part of my life.

00:00:07.019 --> 00:00:08.629
I try to do it as much as I can,

00:00:08.629 --> 00:00:09.899
at least three times a week.

00:00:09.899 --> 00:00:12.260
- I'll do, usually, three days of cardio,

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:13.513
and three days of strength.

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:15.000
- I'm a competitive CrossFitter.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.776
I work out ten or 11 hours a week.

00:00:17.776 --> 00:00:19.747
- For the last four years,

00:00:19.747 --> 00:00:21.747
I've been an Olympic weightlifter.

00:00:21.747 --> 00:00:23.736
- Hopefully I don't, I don't pass out.

00:00:23.736 --> 00:00:25.656
- I don't want to get runner's diarrhea.

00:00:25.656 --> 00:00:27.867
- What if I trip? What
I'm not fast anymore?

00:00:27.867 --> 00:00:28.968
What if I'm too old?

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:32.696
- Best-case scenario, I
beat all the other girls.

00:00:32.696 --> 00:00:35.157
Worst-case scenario, I fail completely

00:00:35.157 --> 00:00:36.957
and make a fool out of myself.

00:00:36.957 --> 00:00:38.877
(ominous, orchestral music)

00:00:38.877 --> 00:00:41.008
- The physical fitness
test is administered

00:00:41.008 --> 00:00:44.258
according to very strict FBI protocols.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:54.106
- Event one, sit-ups to
be done in one minute.

00:00:54.106 --> 00:00:56.564
Event two, 300-meter dash.

00:00:56.564 --> 00:01:00.244
Event three, push-ups to
be done without stopping.

00:01:00.244 --> 00:01:02.698
Event four, one and a half mile run.

00:01:02.698 --> 00:01:06.865
(repetitive, authoritative
orchestral music)

00:01:19.373 --> 00:01:21.562
- You got it.
- Oh my god. Ah!

00:01:21.562 --> 00:01:23.472
That was way harder than I thought.

00:01:23.472 --> 00:01:27.278
(soft, modest music)

00:01:27.278 --> 00:01:29.620
- Sit-ups for time is a lot harder

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:31.340
than I thought it would be.

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:33.079
- I think I did it right.

00:01:33.079 --> 00:01:34.595
I was bouncing pretty hard off the ground.

00:01:34.595 --> 00:01:36.468
I think I got some momentum from that.

00:01:36.468 --> 00:01:37.984
- It wasn't too bad.

00:01:37.984 --> 00:01:41.117
I was very focused
throughout and I feel like

00:01:41.117 --> 00:01:42.744
I'm ready for the next challenge.

00:01:42.744 --> 00:01:44.851
- I went through a range of
emotions, like I'd be like,

00:01:44.851 --> 00:01:48.600
"I'm crushing it! Oh my god
there's so much time left!

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.499
Oh, now I'm slowing... Now
I'm crushing it again!"

00:01:51.499 --> 00:01:55.582
(determined, instrumental music)

00:02:01.478 --> 00:02:04.478
(background cheers)

00:02:13.883 --> 00:02:16.240
(encouraging remarks)

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:19.407
(soft, pulsing music)

00:02:21.371 --> 00:02:22.590
- I went fast out of the gate

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:24.819
and then I was like, this is a bad idea.

00:02:24.819 --> 00:02:28.986
- We got to the half-way mark
and Candace goes, "I'm dying."

00:02:30.139 --> 00:02:32.176
- I felt good, like I went out

00:02:32.176 --> 00:02:33.896
kind of easier --
- Yeah.

00:02:33.896 --> 00:02:35.395
- and then just turned it on.
- Right.

00:02:35.395 --> 00:02:36.915
- But pretty close, I was like,

00:02:36.915 --> 00:02:39.467
am I even running in a
straight direction anymore?

00:02:39.467 --> 00:02:43.634
(escalating, epic orchestral music)

00:03:01.021 --> 00:03:04.702
(soft, tingling percussion)

00:03:04.702 --> 00:03:06.379
- It was pretty easy, because apparently

00:03:06.379 --> 00:03:10.006
FBI push-ups are only
half the range of motion

00:03:10.006 --> 00:03:12.112
compared to the push-ups I normally do.

00:03:12.112 --> 00:03:14.063
- Maybe if I did the correct
form it would have been harder.

00:03:14.063 --> 00:03:18.076
But since I just like
(laughs) screwed it up,

00:03:18.076 --> 00:03:19.317
I think it was pretty easy.

00:03:19.317 --> 00:03:20.923
- It felt really different,
because I normally

00:03:20.923 --> 00:03:23.328
do my push-ups really close here.

00:03:23.328 --> 00:03:25.539
So I felt them a lot in a
different part of my arm.

00:03:25.539 --> 00:03:27.310
- I have a weak upper body,

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:30.288
and I knew that this wasn't gonna be fun.

00:03:30.288 --> 00:03:34.455
(escalating, epic orchestral music)

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:56.880
(soft, pulsing music)

00:03:58.087 --> 00:04:00.518
- I think that slope, that
first slope really hit me

00:04:00.518 --> 00:04:02.918
in my glutes and I felt like
I wasn't going to make it,

00:04:02.918 --> 00:04:04.747
but I kept a consistent pace and

00:04:04.747 --> 00:04:08.014
having the music was really
helpful to get through it.

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:10.200
- At some point I had to
stop and walk a little,

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.811
but then instead of getting defeated,

00:04:11.811 --> 00:04:14.495
I remembered how when I
did marathon training,

00:04:14.495 --> 00:04:18.227
that even a short rest gives
you so much more energy

00:04:18.227 --> 00:04:20.648
and then I was able to take
off and finish the run.

00:04:20.648 --> 00:04:22.736
- I'm actually very
shocked that I did that

00:04:22.736 --> 00:04:24.136
in that amount of time

00:04:24.136 --> 00:04:26.064
because I usually run
like a ten-minute mile.

00:04:26.064 --> 00:04:27.976
I think I was just terrified of failing.

00:04:27.976 --> 00:04:30.016
- Man, that first hill was so steep,

00:04:30.016 --> 00:04:32.294
and I was never the same again.

00:04:32.294 --> 00:04:35.251
But that being said, this was actually

00:04:35.251 --> 00:04:38.883
my fastest mile pace I've run in years.

00:04:38.883 --> 00:04:42.272
(soft instrumental music)

00:04:42.272 --> 00:04:44.294
- So, I passed. I feel good about it.

00:04:44.294 --> 00:04:46.312
I'm slightly surprised.

00:04:46.312 --> 00:04:48.080
I really thought I was going to fail

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:50.590
on that mile and a half run,
so I'm glad that I didn't.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:52.619
- I'm kinda proud of myself.

00:04:52.619 --> 00:04:54.451
I think I did pretty well.

00:04:54.451 --> 00:04:56.711
- The FBI fitness test

00:04:56.711 --> 00:04:59.491
wasn't as challenging as
I thought it was gonna be.

00:04:59.491 --> 00:05:01.350
- But it does make me a little sad

00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:03.710
that I was able to crush the FBI test,

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:05.022
and makes you wonder if they shouldn't

00:05:05.022 --> 00:05:07.182
have a little higher benchmark.

00:05:07.182 --> 00:05:09.755
- Now that I've passed it,
I kinda feel unstoppable.

00:05:09.755 --> 00:05:11.909
I feel like I should be in a
James Bond movie or something.

00:05:11.909 --> 00:05:14.195
- To celebrate, I'm going
to have some ice cream,

00:05:14.195 --> 00:05:16.323
and I'm going to go
work-out in the morning

00:05:16.323 --> 00:05:18.003
feeling pretty good about myself.

00:05:18.003 --> 00:05:21.670
(plucky instrumental music)

